;; D182 regression. os/args is built by a handwritten helper ($rt_os_args)
;; that reaches the vector runtime; the program itself names nothing in the
;; runtime, so the helper-reachability decision must see the helper's own
;; edges or the printer is emitted in its throwing form. No .expected: the
;; output carries this machine's lg path, which the oracle compares live.
(println os/args)
